#TFE Classic "final" release 1.0.#
## Test login info ##
Login: TempImm
Password: llama

(Modern-build note: TempImm is a character in the account "temp", whose
password is also llama. At the greeting's "Choice:" prompt type the character
name TempImm, then the password, then press Return twice. The account menu,
option 1, is only for creating accounts. The game will not boot if
player/TempImm is present but files/accounts has no "temp" account, so the
two files go together. With the RPM, set TFE_SEED_TEST_LOGIN=yes in
/etc/tfe/tfe.env and (re)start tfe.service to add them; see that file.)

The only 3 rooms are those that are needed for the code to run:

#2: Limbo
#9: Default
#33751: Death

The only mob is #31, the blank mob, used as a template for new mobs.

## Source and binaries ##
The source code is obtained from [Seltha](http://seltha.net/tfe/). The TFE Classic Starter kit was modified minimally to get the code to compile on the following machine:
Linux server 2.6.18-308.8.2.el5.centos.plus #1 SMP Tue Jun 12 15:41:32 EDT 2012 x86_64 x86_64 x86_64 GNU/Linux
using c++ (GCC) 4.1.2 20080704 (Red Hat 4.1.2-52)




## Building (modern-build branch) ##
TFE needs a 32-bit build (`-m32`): its scripting engine keeps pointers in `int`.
`make -C src` works with GCC 8 to 14 when the 32-bit glibc and libstdc++
headers are installed (Fedora: `gcc-c++ make glibc-devel.i686 libstdc++-devel.i686`).

`./build.sh` builds `tfe`, `daemon` and an RPM in Podman images (`tfe-base`,
`tfe-build`) into `dist/`. `./build.sh -u` runs a smoke test first (boot the
world, log in as TempImm, shut down from in game); `-b ubi8|ubi9` picks the
builder base; `-r` rebuilds the images. See `./build.sh --help`.

To run by hand, the binaries must be started from a directory beside the data
(`bin/` next to `area/`, `files/`, `player/`, ...), since every path is
`../<dir>/`; see the directory list in `packaging/tfe.tmpfiles`.
The RPM installs `tfe.service` (disabled), running as user `tfe` in
`/var/lib/tfe/bin`, with settings in `/etc/tfe/tfe.env`. Installing does not
start it, and upgrading does not restart it. To use the RPM:

    dnf install tfe-*.x86_64.rpm
    # optional: test login. Set TFE_SEED_TEST_LOGIN=yes in /etc/tfe/tfe.env
    systemctl enable --now tfe
    telnet <host> 4000        # Choice: TempImm   Password: llama

If it will not start, `journalctl -u tfe` says why (status 2 means TFE failed
to boot, and the unit is not restarted). After fixing it:
`systemctl reset-failed tfe; systemctl start tfe`.
